\section{Multi-Node Vacuum Extraction Synchronization}
To prevent spatial metric discontinuities or localized mass-energy deficits,
the micro-void extraction rate $\frac{dM}{dt}$ is synchronized across all MPI
ranks using non-blocking collective operations.

\subsection{Flux Synchronization Model}
Let each node compute a local flux payload:
\[
\bm{F}_i = 
\begin{bmatrix}
dM/dt \\
E_{\text{local}} \\
\Delta_{\text{MOTS}}
\end{bmatrix}.
\]
A non-blocking reduction computes:
\[
\bm{F}_{\text{global}} = \sum_{i=1}^{N} \bm{F}_i.
\]

The global extraction rate is averaged:
\[
\left(\frac{dM}{dt}\right)_{\text{avg}} = 
\frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \left(\frac{dM}{dt}\right)_i.
\]

